mongoc-retry-options-cached - retryReads and retryWrites read from the URI once, when the client is made

Every command asked the client's URI for retryReads and retryWrites (mongoc_uri_get_option_as_bool: a
case-insensitive search of the URI's options), at about ten places in cluster, cmd, cursor and client - several
times per command. A client's URI does not change after it is made, so mongoc_client_t reads both once, beside
enable_overload_retargeting (already read so), and the ten places read the client's copies. The values are the
same: the same option, the same defaults (MONGOC_DEFAULT_RETRYREADS / _RETRYWRITES).

Measured (coraine, mongo 8.2.12, user-space instructions per request, perf stat): PATCH -5,714, retrieve -2,052 (after 0001).

